        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "2e3e084d-4ed0-3382-99ef-5ee58daf1067",
                "word": "romanisme",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e5eace7e-022b-3f29-8e54-df0ef5e5a617",
                        "entry_id": "2e3e084d-4ed0-3382-99ef-5ee58daf1067",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Doctrine de l'Église catholique romaine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "52ae3dbc-5231-4e77-b3aa-c9e0ab9e3fd5",
                                "sense_id": "e5eace7e-022b-3f29-8e54-df0ef5e5a617",
                                "text": "J'y vois [dans Tolède] à chaque pas la plus belle lutte du romanisme et du sémitisme, un élément arabe ou juif qui persiste sous l'épais vernis catholique."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4acb1c25-1df9-3a31-847f-1575fd60127f",
                        "entry_id": "2e3e084d-4ed0-3382-99ef-5ee58daf1067",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Maniérisme romain."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c60ddf77-ebd6-4305-8770-cd9d805869c7",
                                "sense_id": "4acb1c25-1df9-3a31-847f-1575fd60127f",
                                "text": "Le maniérisme gothique des pays du Nord, la peinture provinciale française, le romanisme et le maniérisme tardif néerlandais [sont] autant de mouvements méprisés ou méconnus au temps de la constitution des collections parisiennes."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "60de4d04-dfdb-3637-8fc3-fbd552c0774a",
                        "entry_id": "2e3e084d-4ed0-3382-99ef-5ee58daf1067",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Romanité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2dbb38a8-9f77-4bb6-9002-60086531920d",
                                "sense_id": "60de4d04-dfdb-3637-8fc3-fbd552c0774a",
                                "text": "[Ce livre] contient toute l'aventure du jeune bourgeois alsacien à la caserne allemande, mais ce grand drame moral n'est qu'une scène, dans la longue tragédie qui se joue sur le Rhin entre le Romanisme et la Germanie."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "6b6a0468-6860-4b69-b0e5-95cee80a1474",
                        "source_entry_id": "2e3e084d-4ed0-3382-99ef-5ee58daf1067",
                        "source_sense_description": "catholicisme romain",
                        "target_lang_word": "Romanism",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Romanism",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3c046c9d-2559-3b0c-accf-5c67f123f31f",
                                        "entry_id": "918154d2-dec5-3362-b3d5-022e2aaba788",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The tenets of the Church of Rome; the Roman Catholic religion."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88589747-3ad2-4d1e-b3b6-a9d25de87bbf",
                                                "sense_id": "3c046c9d-2559-3b0c-accf-5c67f123f31f",
                                                "text": "Romanism once extinguished, all other Sects will follow, and that the Catholic Religion—falsely so called—for Catholick means universal—is going, none now will venture to deny."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19c748af-9b6d-4730-bad1-9b0888b402d4",
                                                "sense_id": "3c046c9d-2559-3b0c-accf-5c67f123f31f",
                                                "text": "Then I saw how a spot no larger than this could be crowded with millions of souls, and yet be apparently uninhabited. Romanism increases the degradation of tenantism, and rum completes it."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0e04b81b-1d74-423e-90ec-c7b99d7018a6",
                                                "sense_id": "3c046c9d-2559-3b0c-accf-5c67f123f31f",
                                                "text": "It appears then that Warfield himself really suggests a better way of expressing such differences as obtain between Romanism and Protestantism, or between universalistic and particularistic Protestantism than he has himself employed."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
